\section*{Strongly Balanced Almost-Uniform Vector Permutations}

\subsection{OpenAI's claim}
OpenAI presents the following claims relevant to this question, with manuscript numbers following paper order in Sources. In manuscript 1 (family 097; 2026-09-24), the asserted result is that one signing controls every prescribed-order prefix by $C\sqrt d$, and every zero-sum Euclidean unit-ball family has an ordering with that bound.

\subsection{Mathematical statement of the claimed result}
\paragraph{Manuscript 1.}
For all integers $d,N\ge1$ and vectors $v_1,\ldots,v_N\in\mathbb R^d$ of Euclidean norm at most one, one absolute $C$ is claimed to permit signs with
\[
 \max_{0\le k\le N}\|\sum_{i=1}^k\varepsilon_iv_i\|_2\le C\sqrt d.
\]
The prescribed vector order is retained and the same signs control every prefix. If additionally $\sum_iv_i=0$, the asserted Steinitz--Bergstr\"om consequence instead gives a permutation $\pi$ with
\[
 \max_{0\le k\le N}\|\sum_{i=1}^kv_{\pi(i)}\|_2\le C\sqrt d.
\]
The constant is independent of dimension, vector count and the particular family.

\subsection{Outline of the argument}
For manuscript 1 (family 097; 2026-09-24), a filtered signed walk balances contractions against imposed linear constraints. Matrix trace budgets bound accumulated energy, and Brownian slab estimates turn low energy into shifted signs; a sign-to-ordering reduction gives the zero-sum conclusion.

\subsection{Scope relative to this problem}
The Euclidean theorem supplies an unspecified absolute square-root-dimensional prefix bound after the usual zero-sum augmentation. This problem also prescribes the particular $\sqrt{2.7}$ constant and uniform block controls, which are not asserted by that estimate.

\subsection{Formal verification}
For manuscript 1 (family 097; 2026-09-24), OpenAI lists Lean statements for this assertion: one signing controls every prescribed-order prefix by $C\sqrt d$, and every zero-sum Euclidean unit-ball family has an ordering with that bound.

This coverage does not establish a formal proof of the complete problem as stated here.

The linked family Comparator checks are \texttt{SteinitzBergstrom.lean}.

Their named declarations include \texttt{OAI.EuclideanSteinitzBergstrom.main}.

This site has not executed the Lean code. Described statement coverage is not an independent proof check.

\subsection{Status caveat}
The manuscripts were produced by an internal OpenAI model. OpenAI cautions that results without formalization can contain mistakes. This site has not independently checked the proofs; the label records the scope of OpenAI's claim.

\subsection{Sources}
\begin{itemize}
\item OpenAI, \emph{The Euclidean Steinitz–Bergström theorem}, 2026-09-24; citation key \texttt{OAI:The-Euclidean-Steinitz-Bergstrom-theorem-September-24-2026}. \href{https://github.com/openai/math/blob/adc7f1241b42e322a6451854ab7e4b4c146bf78a/preprints/The-Euclidean-Steinitz-Bergstrom-theorem-September-24-2026/The-Euclidean-Steinitz-Bergstrom-theorem-September-24-2026.pdf}{PDF (GitHub)}; \href{https://github.com/openai/math/raw/adc7f1241b42e322a6451854ab7e4b4c146bf78a/preprints/The-Euclidean-Steinitz-Bergstrom-theorem-September-24-2026/The-Euclidean-Steinitz-Bergstrom-theorem-September-24-2026.pdf}{PDF (direct)}; \href{https://github.com/openai/math/blob/adc7f1241b42e322a6451854ab7e4b4c146bf78a/preprints/The-Euclidean-Steinitz-Bergstrom-theorem-September-24-2026/README.md}{Manuscript page and citation}; \href{https://github.com/openai/math/blob/main/preprints/The-Euclidean-Steinitz-Bergstrom-theorem-September-24-2026/The-Euclidean-Steinitz-Bergstrom-theorem-September-24-2026.pdf}{Latest version}; Statement source: \href{https://github.com/openai/math/blob/adc7f1241b42e322a6451854ab7e4b4c146bf78a/preprints/The-Euclidean-Steinitz-Bergstrom-theorem-September-24-2026/build/introduction.tex\#L10}{thm:signing}.
\item Family 097: \href{https://github.com/openai/math/blob/adc7f1241b42e322a6451854ab7e4b4c146bf78a/lean/docs/097.md}{Lean scope}.
\item \href{https://github.com/openai/math/blob/adc7f1241b42e322a6451854ab7e4b4c146bf78a/lean/ComparatorChallenges/SteinitzBergstrom.json}{Comparator SteinitzBergstrom.json}.
\item \href{https://github.com/openai/math/blob/adc7f1241b42e322a6451854ab7e4b4c146bf78a/lean/ComparatorChallenges/SteinitzBergstrom.lean}{Comparator SteinitzBergstrom.lean}.
